                <pb facs="0425" n="413" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv06/pg413"/>

                <head>Appendix V (D) to CF–65</head>
                <p rendition="#flush">M–261C</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Telegram</p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Roumania</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Special</hi>)</p>
                <p>In accordance with these principles the Hungarian Army has been required to
                    withdraw from Czecho-Slovakia, and the Hungarian Government have been informed
                    that when this is accomplished the Roumanian Army will in its turn withdraw
                    within the new Roumanian borders. It is unnecessary to add that this operation
                    will not be interfered with by Hungarian troops, nor will the latter be allowed
                    to invade Roumanian territory.</p>
                <p>The Allied and Associated Powers feel confident that Roumania will carry out its
                    share of this common policy, thus maintaining unimpaired the solidarity of the
                    Alliance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. Clemenceau</hi></signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-06-13"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >June</hi> 13, 1919</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
